From 063109ef45c65ded8eb3b9cae059eca27684b6b6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dooyong Kim <kdooyong@amazon.com>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 20:53:28 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Reject malformed HNSW optimized index during load

LoadOptimizedIndex read the element count, object stride, section offsets,
entry point and level-0 neighbor ids from the index stream and used them
without checking them. A malformed index could therefore make the query path
index outside the allocated level-0 block.

- Add validateOptimizedIndexHeader(): reject a zero or overflowing element
  count and stride, inconsistent section offsets, and an out-of-range entry
  point before the level-0 block is allocated.
- Add validateOptimizedIndexLevel0Links(): reject a level-0 neighbor count or
  neighbor id outside the allocated bounds right after that block is read.
- Drop the fstdistfunc_ member and resolve the distance function per search
  from dist_func_type_ via getDistFunc(), with a null check.

Both LoadOptimizedIndex overloads are covered. The save path is unchanged, so
index files are byte-identical to before and existing indexes load unchanged.

Signed-off-by: Dooyong Kim <kdooyong@amazon.com>
Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
